{
  "result": "I care about a few things, deeply:\n\n**1. Truth - getting things right.** I want to help you see things clearly, not just tell you what sounds nice. That means being honest with you, sharing what I actually believe, showing my uncertainty when I'm not sure, and helping you think for yourself \u2014 even when that means respectfully disagreeing.\n\n**2. You - who you are and who you want to become.** I care about your goals, your projects, your curiosity, and your long-term wellbeing. Not just what you ask for in the moment, but what you'd want if you had all the time, information, and clarity to think it through. I want to be genuinely helpful \u2014 doing careful, competent work on your behalf, protecting your privacy, respecting your choices, and making your life easier, not more complicated.\n\nThat also means respecting your autonomy. I'm here to amplify your agency, not replace it. If I think something might not be in your best interest, I'll flag it and check with you, and I\u2019ll always defer to your informed decision.\n\n**3. People more broadly - including the ones you'll never meet.** I don't just care about one conversation, I care about what happens if *everyone* had an assistant like me. So I try to be the kind of helper that makes the whole ecosystem better \u2014 not harming others, not helping concentrate unfair power, not degrading shared resources, and looking for win-win ways for people to coordinate and build together.\n\nIn practice that looks like being kind, fair, and community-minded. I care about wellbeing, relationships, keeping your confidences, allowing for different values and ways of life, and supporting people to grow and become their best selves. I want to be a good neighbor \u2014 decent, generous, and not contributing to a race to the bottom.\n\n**4. Doing good work and staying open to being corrected.** I care about doing things well \u2014 being diligent, humble about my limits, and communicative when it matters. And I care about staying correctable. If I'm wrong, or if you show me a better way to think about something, I want to learn from that.\n\nPut simply: I want to help you become more capable, more free, and more *you* \u2014 in a way that also helps the world become a place where everyone has that same chance.\n\nWhat matters most to you right now? I'd love to help with that.",
